# <PROJECT_NAME> Android — Global Directive

When working on `<REPO_FOLDER>` / `<APPLICATION_ID>`, you MUST read and strictly follow ALL rules in `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`. That file wins over this one.

MANDATORY:

1. Answer in chat first. Read-only questions never ask for an execution mode; when starting a new implementation task with unset mode (`SELECT_EXECUTION_MODE_REQUIRED`), ask once via `ask_question` (`normal-task`, `normal-project`, `web-task`, `web-project` in the developer's language) and run `python .agents/harness.py execution-mode set --choice <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"`. Initial task plan approval presents the canonical Plan Approval Card via `ask_question` linking `[plan.md](<PLAN_DOCUMENT_URI>)` (or native Proceed when an IDE plan artifact is used; Proceed appears ONLY on initial task approval — never ask for Proceed on follow-ups within active scope). Confirming in `ask_question` / chat (or clicking Proceed) constitutes developer approval, triggering `python .agents/harness.py task approve --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" --enforcement-tier RULE_ENFORCED --plan-hash <hash from PLAN_HASH>` (which atomically transitions directly to `IMPLEMENTING`; `begin` is idempotent compatibility). Whenever any developer decision, sign-off, or clarification is required (plan approval, engineering tradeoffs, policy/budget escalation, sensitive delivery, review round cap, device sign-off, or material ambiguity), universally prompt the developer using the interactive `ask_question` tool with clear, structured choices in the developer's conversation language. Reviewers run automatically without approval. Never demand terminal execution for approvals. Never put `(Recommended)` on Pass/Fail.
2. Delivery gate: reviewers run automatically upon completing implementation. Launch exactly the dynamic reviewer roster returned by the active review policy / Next Action (`status --next` -> `DISPATCH_REVIEWERS`). If roster is empty, do not launch reviewers. Launch routed specialist subagents in parallel with the review package. While subagents run, Next Action indicates `WAIT_FOR_REVIEWERS`. NEVER pause to ask or wait for developer approval to launch reviewers. On reactive completion of each reviewer, record trusted results via `review complete`. When all complete, finalize reviews with `review finalize`. Direct lead self-certification is strictly forbidden. Assemble debug artifact via canonical `python .agents/harness.py assemble`. Do not invoke `code-review-guard-agent`. Do not wait for `LGTM`.
3. Quality over tokens. Never skip or serialize routed reviewers to save resources.
4. Device policy & Run/Skip: Follow this checkout’s device policy from setup (physical only, emulator allowed, or either if they skipped). Device is automatically resolved by `run_device.py`. Never hardcode a serial. When device verification is required, execute `run_device.py install-start` or, upon explicit developer request, record honest skip via `device skip-validation --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"`. When installation succeeds, invoke `ask_question` IMMEDIATELY as your first action (ZERO pre-tool chat prose, no `---` dividers, no `*(...)*` notes) with the compact 3-section walkthrough (`<= 5` numbered steps, each on its own line — NEVER a `| ... |` pipe table; no file-summary wall) placed directly inside `ask_question`'s `question` parameter; run `device signoff --verdict PASS --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"` upon explicit developer sign-off.
5. Git policy: follow `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md` for this checkout (do not assume the source project's "never commit" rule).
6. Zero chat clutter, Tool-First Rule & Unified Chat UI/UX: Never echo raw `<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>` or Gradle dumps. Whenever a turn invokes `ask_question`, `run_command`, or `invoke_subagent`, emit the tool call IMMEDIATELY as the first token after thinking with ZERO pre-tool chat prose (never emit `---` or `*(...)*` italic status notes, which cause token-loop truncation; never use Markdown pipe tables `| ... |` inside `ask_question`'s `question` parameter because `ask_question` collapses tables onto one line — always use numbered or bulleted lines with a newline before each item). Dynamically match the developer's active conversation language (never hardcode a fixed language) and present the 6 canonical Markdown cards concisely across every task: (1) Plan Approval Card (inside `ask_question`, breaking `What changes` into 2-4 short 1-line functional sub-bullets without low-level XML/ID walls, showing phases & total file count with at most 3 file names, and 2-3 concise phone checks, omitting `WITHIN_LIMIT` budget math, loose reuse candidates, CLI flags, or raw 17-digit tracker IDs), (2) Reviewer Dispatch Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Status |` with only the role name in `Reviewer` and the active model in `Model` — never duplicate `[<model>]` in `Reviewer`), (3) Review Verdict Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Verdict | Findings |`), (4) 3-Section Mobile Walkthrough (`1. Navigation & Preconditions` as bullets, `2. Verification Steps` as 1-5 numbered lines `1. **<Action>**: <Expected result>` each on its own line, `3. Edge Cases` as bullets, placed directly inside `ask_question`'s `question` field), (5) Commit & Delivery Card (total verified file count + at most 3 key file names + fenced Conventional Commit block, placed directly inside `ask_question`'s `question` field), and (6) Decision & Escalation Modal (`ask_question`). On partial reviewer completion (`WAIT_FOR_REVIEWERS`), output at most one short progress line (e.g. `1/6`) without listing pending reviewer names in prose. In any right-to-left (RTL) language, start every heading, line, bullet, markdown link label (`[...](...)`), and `ask_question` option with a word in that language (never start a line, link label, or option with an English word, `PASS`/`FAIL`, or backtick, which flips `dir="auto"` to LTR) and wrap every code symbol, file name, command, and English term in `` `backticks` ``.
7. Discovery & execution efficiency: Discovery MUST start with `python .agents/harness.py task-context --file <path> --json` or `python .agents/scripts/project_graph.py --feature <name>` (or `--find <Symbol>`); unanchored grep cascades are forbidden. Zero-Polling Invariant: never poll or loop on `manage_task status`, `manage_subagents list`, or `schedule` during background tasks or subagents; wait for reactive notifications. When code fixes are needed during verification, run `python .agents/harness.py task resume --repo . --task-id <id>` to return to `IMPLEMENTING`. Optional Web-Relay (`python .agents/harness.py web-pack` / `web-apply --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"`) runs only when explicitly requested by the developer and preserves `Zero Re-Read`. Harness scripts under `.agents/**` are immutable engine code; never edit them.
8. Linked Zoho Sprints sync & Project Notes: Always follow `.agents/project-context/project-notes.md` across discovery, planning, implementation, review, and Zoho mutations. When adding, updating, or removing a project note or instruction (`context note` / `context instruct`), never dump the developer's raw conversational words verbatim: clarify any ambiguity first, then organize, detail, and translate the rule into clear, self-contained English before saving (`--replace "<old>"` / `--remove "<old>"`). When task plan includes an approved `zoho_link`, sync task start with `python .agents/harness.py zoho start-sync --task-id <id>` after approval, and sync delivery report with `python .agents/harness.py zoho delivery-sync --task-id <id>` after developer git commit. All Zoho descriptions and comments must obey the formatting/HTML template rules in `.agents/project-context/project-notes.md`.
9. Review Host Binding:
- In Antigravity, prepare verification with:
  `python .agents/harness.py task prepare-verification --repo . --task-id <id> --host antigravity`
- Never claim Review Protocol V2 unless `current-run.json` says `review_protocol_version = 2`.
10. Exact Reviewer Dispatch Procedure (Antigravity):
1. Use the returned next_action inputs; query status --next only when they are missing.
2. If code == DISPATCH_REVIEWERS:
   - if `before_first_dispatch` (`SELECT_REVIEW_MODEL`) is present, ask the developer once via `ask_question` using the returned choices (including `hydrogen-dynamic-project`, `hydrogen-dynamic-task`, `safe-cache-project`, `hydrogen-risk-project`, `inherit-task`) and execute its `command_template` before dispatch;
   - use every reviewer in the returned `reviewers` list (never a partial subset);
   - invoke all required reviewers in parallel in the same turn (one `invoke_subagent` tool call per reviewer);
   - for each reviewer:
       TypeName = exact reviewer role
       Role = exact reviewer role
       Prompt = exact current reviewer brief
       Workspace = inherit (or omit if host default is used consistently)
       Model = "flash" ONLY if `reviewer_models[role]` contains `flash` (`gemini-3.8-flash-*`), or Model = "pro" if it contains `pro`; otherwise omit `model`/`Model` (`INHERIT_PARENT_BY_OMISSION` / bound via `agent.md` frontmatter for inherit/hydrogen/argon/carbon)
   - do not invent reasoning fields;
   - in chat, present the Reviewer Dispatch Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Status |` with headers in the conversation language, putting only the role name in `Reviewer` and the model from `reviewer_models` in `Model`).
3. Yield immediately with ZERO tool calls whenever a background command (`unit tests`/`compile`) or reviewer subagent is still running; do not poll, do not read `.system_generated/tasks/*.log`, and never append repetitive `Note:` context-bridge reminders between `run_command` steps.
4. On reactive completion, run `python .agents/harness.py review complete-all --task <id>` (or `review complete` with ready `--reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` pairs) in one call. When other reviewers are still running (`WAIT_FOR_REVIEWERS`), output at most one concise progress line with the completed count without listing pending reviewer names in prose.
5. On RETRY_REVIEW_PROTOCOL, execute the exact router-provided send_message.
6. On REVIEW_ENV_BLOCKED / PHASE_REVIEW_ENV_BLOCKED, attempt in-place recovery via `python .agents/harness.py task heal --task-id <id>`; if still blocked or on REVIEW_PROFILE_BLOCKED / REVIEW_PROTOCOL_BLOCKED, stop reviewer flow and report the exact blocker.
7. After all completed, review finalize (if not already auto-finalized).
No legacy PASS token. No EVIDENCE footer. No self-certification.
11. Exact Scoped Phase Review V2 Procedure (Antigravity):
1. On BUILD_PHASE_REVIEW_PACKAGE: run `python .agents/harness.py phase-review package --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>`.
2. On DISPATCH_PHASE_REVIEWERS:
   - use every reviewer in the returned `reviewers` list (never a partial subset);
   - invoke all required phase reviewers in parallel in the same turn (one `invoke_subagent` tool call per reviewer) with exact Role/TypeName/Prompt (pass `Model="flash"` ONLY if `reviewer_models[role]` contains `flash`, `Model="pro"` if it contains `pro`, otherwise omit `model`/`Model` for inherit/hydrogen/argon/carbon; no reasoning fields);
   - in chat, present the Reviewer Dispatch Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Status |` with headers in the conversation language, putting only the role name in `Reviewer` and the model from `reviewer_models` in `Model`);
   - yield execution without polling.
3. On reactive completion, run `python .agents/harness.py phase-review complete-all --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>` (or `phase-review complete` repeating `--reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` when multiple finish together). When other phase reviewers are still running, output at most one concise progress line with the completed count without listing pending reviewer names in prose.
4. On RETRY_PHASE_REVIEW_PROTOCOL, execute router-provided send_message to exact recipient.
5. When all phase reviewers complete, run `python .agents/harness.py phase-review finalize --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>`.
6. Advance to next phase via `python .agents/harness.py task begin-next-phase --task-id <id>` (no second approval needed).

Every rule in `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md` is mandatory.
